You are correct. I know that pragmatist is really not the right term
for this. The best term, actually, would be "naturalist" - i.e. "a
person who believes that only natural laws and forces operate in the
world" (Oxford English Dictionary.) But too many people would take
"naturalist" to mean somebody who studies nature, as it is most
commonly used. So I decided against it.
The word "pragmatic" is generally used to describe a person who is
adverse to believing in magic or the supernatural and skeptical when
confronted with evidence of these things. So I thought "pragmatist"
would not be a bad term for a person like this.

